 "construction": "Sleek, from the Pass 1 gun (kept: truncated-cone pedestal with a narrow neck, angular wedge receiver, a dark jacket that carries the barrel line, continuous light). New: LAYERED armour - ceramic shells stand off a dark frame on the pedestal, the yoke, the cheeks and along the jacket; the barrel is a twin-rail emitter with a lit slot, so the weapon reads as one 0.5 m line from breech to muzzle; faceted yoke with lit trunnions; light chevrons on the top rail (from the Pass 2 gun and the reference); the phase ring rides the jacket and slides on recoil",
 "style_character": "advanced technology: smooth compound housings, lacquer / ceramic, graphite frames, light strips and rings",
